# Read by Wrangler, which loads .env into its environment before every command.
#
# An empty CLOUDFLARE_ENV selects the top-level environment in wrangler.jsonc,
# the same as passing `--env=""`. Without it, Wrangler warns on every deploy
# once wrangler.jsonc defines any named environment under `env`. An explicit
# `--env <name>` still wins, so `wrangler deploy --env beta` is unaffected.
#
# Committed on purpose, so the Cloudflare build gets it too. Next.js and Vite
# also load .env, but the variable has no public prefix and never reaches the
# client bundle. Do not put secrets here: this file is in git. Use .env.local
# or .dev.vars for those.
CLOUDFLARE_ENV=
